(747402, 80692, 12448, '<td valign="top">Not sure exactly what you are going for here.  The feeling I get is the US and Britain taking a chance on the roll of the dice and .......??????????  If you are talking about the team effort to go to war, I''m sorry, that is not a sport by any stretch of the imagination.  A very nice shot, not sure why the spring is there, nor the dice, technically, very well done, but overall appeal, not really there.  And since I can''t really figure out the team/sport aspect (which is what I thought the challenge was supposed to be about) I''m sitting at a 3 on this one unless I can figure this out.</td>', 'Not sure exactly what you are going for here.  The feeling I get is the US and Britain taking a chance on the roll of the dice and .......??????????  If you are talking about the team effort to go to war, I''m sorry, that is not a sport by any stretch of the imagination.  A very nice shot, not sure why the spring is there, nor the dice, technically, very well done, but overall appeal, not really there.  And since I can''t really figure out the team/sport aspect (which is what I thought the challenge was supposed to be about) I''m sitting at a 3 on this one unless I can figure this out.', '2004-06-02 15:58:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(747408, 80814, 7152, '<td valign="top">Sweet .. I wanted to do something like this .. except there is no where I could find a car like this ... oh .. how I would love to sit in that an floor it ... if you''ve driven that thing PLEASEEEEE message me and tell me how it is. <br/>The composition is great .. but it seems to me that the camera wasn''t straight (the car looks on a angle). 10</td>', 'Sweet .. I wanted to do something like this .. except there is no where I could find a car like this ... oh .. how I would love to sit in that an floor it ... if you''ve driven that thing PLEASEEEEE message me and tell me how it is. The composition is great .. but it seems to me that the camera wasn''t straight (the car looks on a angle). 10', '2004-06-02 16:04:01.000000', NULL, 1),
