(757494, 80461, 22011, '<td valign="top">Hi-ho,<br/> <br/>Thanks for all your comments...<br/> <br/>I was intending to have a shot of the shirts against a bright blue sky, or sunset, but by the time I got around to takin the shot it was the last day, and heavily overcast.  Nothing I took outside looked any good, and I ran out of light so I moved into the garage.<br/> <br/>I figured this would be better than nothing, although I probably should have made more effort with the sheet/background and the voting reflects that.. Such is life :-).<br/> <br/>Not too sure if I could have improved the numbers all that much, the floods used are diffused (24" round 400W each), but I don''t have any large reflectors.  Might have to get some sheets of white something to hang in the garage. :-).  The numbers themselves are made of a shiny iron-on plastic, even in the day light shots I took they picked up some heavy reflections.<br/> <br/>Cheers, Me.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-06-09 16:37:15.</i></td>', 'Hi-ho, Thanks for all your comments... I was intending to have a shot of the shirts against a bright blue sky, or sunset, but by the time I got around to takin the shot it was the last day, and heavily overcast.  Nothing I took outside looked any good, and I ran out of light so I moved into the garage. I figured this would be better than nothing, although I probably should have made more effort with the sheet/background and the voting reflects that.. Such is life :-). Not too sure if I could have improved the numbers all that much, the floods used are diffused (24" round 400W each), but I don''t have any large reflectors.  Might have to get some sheets of white something to hang in the garage. :-).  The numbers themselves are made of a shiny iron-on plastic, even in the day light shots I took they picked up some heavy reflections. Cheers, Me.', '2004-06-09 17:29:39.000000', '2004-06-09 17:37:15.000000', 0),
(757499, 80261, 8054, '<td valign="top">Very nice image but I see two flaws that would have prevented me from giving this a 10. First is that big white spot in the upper left corner. That is very distracting and should have been cropped out. The second flaw is not as major but is noticeable and that the image is slightly tilted towards the left. I do like the duotone/sepia look and I agree that it gives it a very timeless feel. Looks nicely focused and details are sharp. I would have given this a 7. Good job overall and congrats on your ribbon!</td>', 'Very nice image but I see two flaws that would have prevented me from giving this a 10. First is that big white spot in the upper left corner. That is very distracting and should have been cropped out. The second flaw is not as major but is noticeable and that the image is slightly tilted towards the left. I do like the duotone/sepia look and I agree that it gives it a very timeless feel. Looks nicely focused and details are sharp. I would have given this a 7. Good job overall and congrats on your ribbon!', '2004-06-09 17:30:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(757519, 80131, 18529, '<td valign="top">I love the photo!  Personally, I would have named it GOOOOOOOOOOOAAAAAAAAAAALLLLLLLL!  Just a thought.</td>', 'I love the photo!  Personally, I would have named it GOOOOOOOOOOOAAAAAAAAAAALLLLLLLL!  Just a thought.', '2004-06-09 17:47:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(757531, 80261, 18529, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by MrAkamai:</b></div><hr/><i> Very nice image but I see two flaws that would have prevented me from giving this a 10. First is that big white spot in the upper left corner. That is very distracting and should have been cropped out. The second flaw is not as major but is noticeable and that the image is slightly tilted towards the left. I do like the duotone/sepia look and I agree that it gives it a very timeless feel. Looks nicely focused and details are sharp. I would have given this a 7. Good job overall and congrats on your ribbon! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>My opinion is just the opposite.  I love the white corner, I think it gives it shape and feel for the room.  Also, I am not noticing the tilt either.  I would have given this a 20 if it were possible.</td>', 'Originally posted by MrAkamai: Very nice image but I see two flaws that would have prevented me from giving this a 10. First is that big white spot in the upper left corner. That is very distracting and should have been cropped out. The second flaw is not as major but is noticeable and that the image is slightly tilted towards the left. I do like the duotone/sepia look and I agree that it gives it a very timeless feel. Looks nicely focused and details are sharp. I would have given this a 7. Good job overall and congrats on your ribbon!  My opinion is just the opposite.  I love the white corner, I think it gives it shape and feel for the room.  Also, I am not noticing the tilt either.  I would have given this a 20 if it were possible.', '2004-06-09 17:52:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(757559, 80279, 21711, '<td valign="top">i think the 3 people who voted 10 on this should explain to us what this image is portraying<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-06-10 09:36:39.</i></td>', 'i think the 3 people who voted 10 on this should explain to us what this image is portraying', '2004-06-09 18:12:05.000000', '2004-06-10 10:36:39.000000', 0),
